    return -EINVAL;
...
bit_cfg = config_pins[wi_order];
Reason:
The validation condition uses `>` instead of `>=`, so `wire_order[i]` is allowed to equal `ARRAY_SIZE(config_pins)` (which is 4 for an array of size 4). This value is then used as an index into `config_pins[]`, causing an out-of-bounds read because valid indices are only 0–3.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
if (WARN_ON(wire_order[i] >= ARRAY_SIZE(config_pins)))
    return -EINVAL;
Reason:
Changing the comparison to `>=` ensures that only indices 0 through `ARRAY_SIZE(config_pins)-1` (i.e., 0–3) are accepted, preventing any out-of-bounds access when `config_pins[wi_order]` is later used.

